## Quick Reference

### Most Common Commands
```bash
# Development workflow
./src/scripts/setup.sh dev                    # Setup dev environment
./src/scripts/migrate.sh up dev               # Apply migrations
./src/scripts/deploy.sh dev deploy            # Deploy to dev

# Migration management
./src/scripts/migrate.sh create name dev      # Create migration
./src/scripts/migrate.sh validate             # Validate migrations
./src/scripts/migrate.sh test name dev        # Test migration

# Deployment
./src/scripts/deploy.sh dev status            # Check status
./src/scripts/deploy.sh dev logs              # View logs
./src/scripts/deploy.sh dev generate          # Generate spec
```

### Environment-Specific
```bash
# Development
./src/scripts/setup.sh dev
./src/scripts/migrate.sh up dev
./src/scripts/deploy.sh dev deploy

# Staging
./src/scripts/setup.sh staging
./src/scripts/migrate.sh up staging
./src/scripts/deploy.sh staging deploy

# Production
./src/scripts/setup.sh prod
./src/scripts/migrate.sh up prod
./src/scripts/deploy.sh prod deploy
```

## Notes

- **Always use scripts**: Never create migrations manually or use tools directly
- **Test in dev first**: Always test changes in development before staging/production
- **Validate before commit**: Run validation commands before committing migrations
- **Check status**: Use status commands to verify current state
- **Debug mode**: Enable DEBUG=true for troubleshooting
- **Test before commit** when possible
- **Provide clear feedback** on command execution
- **Stop on errors** and report issues clearly
- **Confirm destructive operations** before execution